system on it and a 4-gb drive for user files.

We keep getting a message in the console that says the  
available swap space is below 10%.  We have had to reboot  
the system a few times after it hung, and I am assuming  
that this is related to the low swap space.

Is there a relatively simple way to increase the amount of  
swap space, or can this only be done when installing the  
operating system?  If the current system can be modified,  
where should I look for instructions on doing this?  Is it  
