From:  Jim Skoog (skoog@netcom.com)
Re:    High Traffic Web Site Performance

Where are the performance bottlenecks for Alpha AXP running the
Netscape Commerce Server 1.12 with high volume internet traffic?  
We are evaluating network performance for a variety of Alpha AXP 
runing DEC UNIX 3.2C, which run DEC's seal firewall and behind
that Alpha 1000 and 2100 webservers.  Some of these machines have 
fddi network controllers, others have only tulip or lance ethernet
controllers. Due to security restrictions, logging is not allowed.
So instead of monitoring or running benchmarks (too costly),
perhaps some of you with experience and access have already 
identified performance problems.  I know from maintaining a read 
news feed that CPU, and extra inodes per filesystem were problems
to be overcome.  I suspect that CPU or network traffic are the
bottlenecks.





