Assuming you have the legal right to do so, you can often use "dd" to copy
the master disk to the CD writer.  Unless you are changing the format of the
data on the disk, there is no need to remaster the contents.

Dave

PS - if your systems are networked, consider using RIS to do network
installs.  You'll only need one copy of the media to do this.

