running well for more than 8 months without a problem. In fact it is STILL
running without fail except for the following:

We cannot reach a specific host name: IBMMAIL.COM

If I launch nslookup and query IBMMAIL.COM, I get no responce. If I tell
nslookup to use some other server (for example our secondary dns server
maintained by our upstream provider) it works. I can get the MX records
and see the needed IP addresses. If I point nslookup to the master DNS
server for IBMMAIL.COM (which is WATSON.IBM.COM) I get the same result.
