SOME OF THE NEW FEATURES:

- Easier integration: X/bigX starts the local X Window server;
- Product feature xkeymapx for assigning individual keyboard mappings to
  (groups of) applications;
- Support of the protocol extensions XTestExtension1 and DOUBLE-BUFFER;
- Transparent and secure authorization methods;
- New configurable workarounds compensating for bugs of certain X Window
  clients and servers;
- Increased performance;
- Added platform support: Digital UNIX (DEC OSF/1, Alpha) 3.2 and 4.0 and IBM
  AIX (Power and PowerPC) from 3.2.5 on.



WHAT IS X/bigX?

The X/bigX base product combines the screens of one X Window server to one or
several larger so-called meta-screens. The screens of a meta-screen can be
arbitrarily arranged: partly or totally overlapping, with gaps, totally filling
the meta-screen, etc.

The functionality of the base product X/bigX may be enhanced by additional
product features:

- X/bigX/multiServer is able to control multiple X Window servers,
  workstations, X terminals or X-enabled PCs.
- X/bigX/dynamicServer comprises multiServer and provides for connecting and
  disconnecting X Window servers during runtime.
- X/bigX/failsafe comprises dynamicServer and provides a highly available X
  Window server: X/bigX/failsafe detects the breakdown of one, multiple or even
  all X Window servers and does not interrupt the X Window clients.
- X/bigX/xie in addition supports the XIE X Image Extension.
- The product feature xkeymapx allows to assign different keyboard mappings to
  single X Window applications.

The GUI configuration tool X/bigX/tool is included with X/bigX/dynamicServer.
Nearly each aspect of X/bigX can be configured on the command line, in a
configuration file or through X/bigX/tool (X/bigX understands 29 statements
and 21 per (meta-)screen sub-statements).

X/bigX is not ...

- a proprietary X Window server: X/bigX cooperates with the usual X Window
  servers and fully utilizes their capabilities including hardware
  acceleration.
- a specialized window manager: X/bigX is totally transparent to all X Window
  clients including window managers and therefore can be integrated very easily
  into environments like CDE, OSF/Motif, VUE, or OpenWindows.

Some of X/bigX's application areas:

- process visualization and control,
- medical imaging,
- trading systems,
- network management,
- GIS,
- EDA,
- CAD,
- software development.

X/bigX is available for the following operating systems:

- Digital UNIX (DEC OSF/1, Alpha) from 3.2 on,
- Hewlett-Packard HP-UX 9 (PA-RISC),
- Hewlett-Packard HP-UX 10 (PA-RISC),
- IBM AIX (Power and PowerPC) from 3.2 on,
- Sun Solaris 1 (SunOS 4, SPARC) from 1.1 on,
- Sun Solaris 2 (SunOS 5, SPARC) from 2.3 on,
- Sun Solaris 2 (SunOS 5, x86) from 2.4 on.



