In article <4oi429$kvu@condor.ic.net>, Harold Todd Chapman <htchapma@oakland.edu> writes:
|>I am trying to run a software package that needs libcxx.so
|>
|>Where can I get this from? I can't seem to find it in the subsets.
|>
|>-Thanks
|>
|>

Prior to Digital UNIX V4.0 (which has it in OSFBASE400), this shared library is
part of the DEC C++ Class Library, Run-Time Support subset (CXXSHRDA).  This 
subset is not part of the Digital UNIX base o/s product.  On your distribution 
media, look for the "DEC_C++_RTL" directory which contains this subset.

