organization: Performance Software Limited
reply-to: mje@psldev.psl.co.uk
newsgroups: comp.unix.osf.osf1


We are porting some streams modules from Solaris 2.3/4/5 and AT&T MP-RAS 
SVR4 to Digital UNIX and have come across a perculiarity in the Digital 
UNIX implementation.

The kernel entry points for a streams module (not driver) are 
xx_configure, xx_open and xx_close where xx is the name of your module. 
The xx_open module is passed a pointer to a dev_t which should contain 
the major and minor device numbers for the device being opened. On 
Solaris and AT&T this is OK but on Digital UNIX the dev_t pointer is 
always NULL.

Has anyone else come across the strange problem and maybe knows the 
solution? Our modules will not function without the device major/minor 
numbers and we are less than a month away from the deadline for code 
completion of this port.

