Try using restore -s 2 -t for the second dump file, see the restore man page.
We have used dump/restore here (I espescially like restore -i) for about a
year and have been quite happy with the result.


My understanding is that the feet left on a tape is computed after each
dump command without knowlwdge of previous files on the tape. Better would
be a tape % so you can see what you've used/have. Some assumptions are made
about tape length, density so it may not be exact for your setup. I just
ignore it.

