>>>>> "DANIEL" == DANIEL GLAUSER A <dglauser@el3.cs.umass.edu> writes:

    DANIEL>    Should I be using vdump and vrestore for the UFS
    DANIEL> partition?  I know I must use these commands for the
    DANIEL> AdvUFS partitions.

You can use vdump/vrestore for both UFS and AdvFS. You can NOT use
dump on AdvFS.

    DANIEL>    If you have multiple backups on one tape, restore
    DANIEL> allows you to skip n number with the -s switch.  What is
    DANIEL> the equivalent for vrestore?  I could not find it.

Unfortunately vrestore still hasn't got a -s switch. What I usually do
is use the 'mt fsf' command to position the tape. Don't forget to
always use the no rewind device. One complication is that if you have
a backup of an empty fileset that you want to skip over, you don't need
to do a mt command to skip to the next set (you're already positioned
correctly then).

    DANIEL>    rmt0h is the traditional (no rewind) device, correct?

nrmt0h is the no-rewind device.

