In article <4nvari$7ck@crcnis3.unl.edu> schaffin@unlinfo.unl.edu (scott chaffin) writes:

  Scott> Does anyone know if Digital plans to support more than 256
  Scott> colors at any time in the future?  Currently, most graphics
  Scott> applications (such as Netscape...) look much better on a
  Scott> $3,000 PC than on the $15,000 workstation I just set up.
  Scott> Does the Alpha version of Linux have better color support?

You didn't say what graphics card it is.  If it's a TGA (21030 chip),
then I think you're out of luck.  If it's an S3 or Mach64 based card,
then Linux/Alpha will indeed support a 16bpp mode.  I'm running a #9
GXE 64 in this mode and it works quite nicely.  There are a few bugs
left in the XFree port to the Alpha that manifest themselves in a few
pixels being drawn too much occasionally, but they are not fatal and
are being worked on by the XFree folks.

