In article <31A3591A.41C6@paneer.ndim.edrc.cmu.edu> sean levy <snl@paneer.ndim.edrc.cmu.edu> writes:
>under osf/1 [at least as of 3.2c, which is what i'm running] pthread_t is
>a struct, not a pointer or integer. this is the worst of the interface
>incompatibilities between dec's implementation and all others i've seen
>so far, which don't hand structures around by value.

That's because we introduced POSIX threads very early and hence were
based on an early draft of the standard (draft 4). In Digital UNIX V4.0
you get the 1003.1C interfaces and pthread_t is a pointer.

