Eric Werme (werme@alingo.zk3.dec.com) wrote:
: >I'm getting the following error message after installing Digital Unix 3.2D-2
: >when ever any application tries to use flock():
: >fnctl: Local lock-manager not registered
: You need to be running rpc.lockd on both your NFS client and server.  (This
: should only be happening for NFS files.)  You also need rpc.statd and portmap.
: Best thing to do is run nfssetup and agree to its suggestion to run lockd and
: statd.

Thanks for all those who suggested I run lockd and statd.  I was starting
them up, but they were dying due to strangeness in my DNS setup (for some
reason they didn't like resolving my ip address and promptly gave up).  I've
fixed the problems and NFS locking is working great!

Next problem: Has anyone gotten Majordomo working on Digital Unix?  One of
our students has been working at it and keeps sucking up all the memory on
our AlphaServer 2100 in the process.

