Hi.  I'm having problems trying to get a CDROM tower to work on an
AlphaServer 2000 with a StorageWorks RAID Array 200 controller.

The system:

DEC AlphaServer 2000 running OSF/1 v3.2
StorageWorks RAID Array 200 3-channel controller in EISA slot 1
StorageWorks RAID Array 200 1-channel controller in EISA slot 6
EISA video card
PCI network adapter
Plextor Quad Speed Hot Swap CDROM Tower with 7 4Plex-256 CDROM drives

The problems:

The 1-channel RAID Array was purchased along with the Plextor CDROM tower
(yes, I know it's overkill..I didn't order it).  When trying to install/
configure the RAID Array, I received an error/warning after copying CFG
file from inside the ECU.  The warning said that a copy of the file already
existed, and I should select the "Copy Files" option from the Main Menu.
There is no "Copy Files" option on the ECU Main Menu, so I ignored that.
I believe the warning came up because the main SCSI controller in the system
is another RAID Array 200, and its configuration file is already installed.

After configuring the ECU, which appears to have gone well aside from the
error mentioned above, I restarted the system and ran the RAID Array 200
Standalone Configuration Utility.  According to the instructions in the
RAID Array manual, I should have been able to select "Auto Configure" and
configure the CDROM devices in JBOD (Just a Bunch Of Disks) mode.  This is
how the other SCSI devices connected to the 3-channel controller are
configured.  However, when I select "Auto Configure", it tells me that either
there are no devices connected, or the devices do not support this function.

When I tried to manually configure, I was able once to get information
about each device (reported correctly as Plextor CDROMs), but not able to
group the devices in any way.  After changing the ECU configuration options
regarding spinup and taggin, I was unable to even get that information.

So, what I'm wondering, is if anyone has had any experience using the RAID
Array 200 with CDROMs, either with a tower, or with a single CDROM device
(the AlphaServer comes with one, so I imagine they are compatible).  Also,
is anyone using multiple RAID Array 200s like this?

I'm going to test the Plextor tower on a Novell server which is currently
configured using another Plextor tower, to make sure it's operating correctly
and there isn't a cable problem, meanwhile.

Any help would be greatly appreciated.

Thanks,
Jim

