Mitzi Adams ES82 <adamsml@magaxp1.msfc.nasa.gov> wrote:
>I am increasingly annoyed by having to click a mouse button to
>intitialize a window.  Is there an application for the alpha which will
>follow the mouse and activate whatever window in which the mouse is? I
>know there is such an application for the PC.  
>
>Thanks!
>Mitzi Adams
>adamsml@magaxp1.msfc.nasa.gov

Hi Mitzi
Well you don't have to do anything but change your .Xdefaults file.  
Assuming you are using Motif, you should find a line like

 Mwm*keyboardFocusPolicy:  explicit
Change this to
 Mwm*keyboardFocusPolicy:  pointer

Then whatever window the mouse is in will recive input.   I think that 
was your question.  

