In article <DrG4wn.DLL@uia.ua.ac.be>, dbruyne@uia.ua.ac.be (Karel.DeBruyne) writes:

|> I have a SparcStation 10 running Solaris 2.4 and CDE.
|> Most of the colors needed by asWedit are not available when I want to
|> start it.
|> I am sure this isn't a problem of asWedit but it stops me from evaluating
|> asWedit.
|>
|> Does anyone know how to solve this.

From the on-line FAQ (Program startup):

[Q] Upon startup, I get a large number of messages that say
        Warning: Cannot allocate colormap entry for "xxxxx"
    where xxxxx is a specific color. What's wrong ?
[A] Are you using Netscape Navigator (Netscape) or other graphics programs
    that require a lot of colors ?
    Netscape can be quite demanding on colors (especially if you view
    colorful pages ...).
    The possible solutions are:
    1. Start asWedit before Netscape.
    2. Start Netscape and tell it to use a private colormap, i.e. start it as:
        netscape -install
       After this *all* other programs still can use the default colormap.
       Note that you might see unpleasant colormap flashing when
       switching between applications using different colormaps.
    3. Limit the number of colors Netscape will allocate from the default
       colormap using '-ncols' command option when Netscape is started
       (note that value 0 tells Netscape to allocate as many colors it can
       get!).
       To see all possible command options start Netscape with the "-help"
       flag (the same goes for asWedit).

Try the above solutions and choose the best one for your setup.
BTW, the default colors for asWedit HTML color tags have been chosen for
displays using Gamma correction (on our displays we use Gamma between 1.4
and 1.7).


