We have another, distinct C compiler problem. The generated code
seg faults at run-time, apparently due to an extraneous instruction
in a common return sequence using 't12' - a temporary register. 
This is dUNIX V3.2C/D with OSFCMPLRS350/360. I have tried various
optimisations, with and without debug, to no avail. OSFCMPLRS200 works,
generating similar code, but without the offending instruction.

Bad code:

0x120005d30 <output_line+2144>: 263dffff  9     ldah    a1, -65536(gp)
0x120005d34 <output_line+2148>: 22317b10  8     lda     a1, 31504(a1)
0x120005d38 <output_line+2152>: a77d8388 29     ldq     t12, -31864(gp)
0x120005d3c <output_line+2156>: 6b5b7d9c 1a     jsr     ra, (t12),
0x1200053b0
0x120005d40 <output_line+2160>: 27ba2000  9     ldah    gp,
536870912(ra)
0x120005d44 <output_line+2164>: 23bd4e90  8     lda     gp, 20112(gp)
** Common return code **
0x120005d48 <output_line+2168>:
    c3e00000 30 br      zero, 0x120005d4c <output_line+2172>
** Silly instruction **
0x120005d4c <output_line+2172>: a73be5b0 29     ldq     t11, -6736(t12)
**
0x120005d50 <output_line+2176>: 275e0001  9     ldah    ra, 65536(sp)
0x120005d54 <output_line+2180>: a75a09f0 29     ldq     ra, 2544(ra)
0x120005d58 <output_line+2184>: 253e0001  9     ldah    s0, 65536(sp)
0x120005d5c <output_line+2188>: a52909f8 29     ldq     s0, 2552(s0)
0x120005d60 <output_line+2192>: 279e0001  9     ldah    at, 65536(sp)
0x120005d64 <output_line+2196>: 23dc0a50  8     lda     sp, 2640(at)
0x120005d68 <output_line+2200>: 6bfa8001 1a     ret     zero, (ra), 1


Good code from OSFCMPLRS200:

0x120005af0 <output_line+2128>: a6100000 29     ldq     a0, 0(a0)
0x120005af4 <output_line+2132>: a63d8028 29     ldq     a1, -32728(gp)
0x120005af8 <output_line+2136>: 223183d0  8     lda     a1, -31792(a1)
0x120005afc <output_line+2140>: a77d8440 29     ldq     t12, -31680(gp)
