Juergen Schroeder (schroedj@ub.uni-marburg.de) wrote:
: Vasco Lopes Paulo (vlp@amadeus.inesc.pt) wrote:
: : 
: : I have some new AlphaStations 200 all with 19" screens with (I think)
: : standard graphic cards.
: : 
: : On digital unix this can't be done through the SRM Console commands so
: : I sticked to the 1024x768  resolution.
: : What should I do to change to a 1280x1024 resolution, using X11?
: : 
: : My guess is that I have to create a new kernel, replacing the tga0
: : controller by some thing else... Which I don't know what it is...
: 
: On my 200 with an ZLXp Card I had only to use the dip swiches on the  card,
: X  recognize this and change the resolution. Look on the manual of the card
: for the settings.

Assuming your card supports the resolution, and you have the X server
set installed with the driver etc etc:

/var/X11/xdm/Xservers

Add the argument: -screen0 NNNN

I.E.

:0 local /usr/bin/X11/X -nice -2 -screen0 1280

Curt Smith
curts@compgen.com




