attempt at a description of this device is, it is a PC-like device, whats works
like an X (or anything else) terminal, but has it's own disk etc etc. Look at DEC's
page for a better description - I'm not a DEC man myself (hate the stuff - personal
opinion) but this device _sounded_ quite a good idea from the configuration (ie
sysadm) point of view.

