I alway have discrepencies with the output of feet on the tape and have 
found that I dislike the restore -t command.

Instead I use the "mt fsf number".  Where number is the backup you want to 
go to the end of.  In your case rewind the tape then "mt fsf 1"  would put 
you at the end of the first filesystem backed up (Hmmm, check the mt man 
page it may advance 1 filesystem and you could do this incrementally as 
you check). 

Then I usually do a "restore -i" (interactive) to view what's there.  I 
think the command is "what" and it will display the tape header (the 
filesystem you back up) like / or /usr.  At the interactive prompt type in 
a ? to get a list of commands that give you info (like ls).

Good luck.



