	Folks there is a known bug, a "Race condition", in the Xserver
for the PXG boards.  DEC was unable to fix it and when I last checked
the fix was to upgrade to a ZLX series board.

	Yes, it is annoying.  You can restart the Xserver with the following
command or a variation on it;

#!/bin/sh
ps -eaf | grep "/usr/bin/X11/X " | gawk '{print "kill -9 "$2}'|sh

	Netscape and some backgrounds will do it regularly, prior to 
netscape, double clicking an icon or unusual graphics would trigger it
occasionally.

	Calling the following in cron is reputed to help somewhat.  It
certainly doesn't cure the problem, though it may make it less
frequent.

#!/bin/csh
/usr/bin/ipcs -m | /sbin/grep "m "| /usr/bin/awk '{ printf("ipcrm -m %d\n",$2);
'  | /sbin/sh




	All the best,

		Peter David






