I don't use elm (I use exmh), so I can't reply specifically, but DU
3.2 includes a passable C compiler. But 4.0 will include the better,
currently unbundled one. I have used cc on 3.2 to build perl and a
number of other packages, though I also use gcc frequently.

Porting to DU is slightly more difficult because DU is 64 bit. and
that means that long != int. This is a tacit assumption in a lot of
popular code. There are also problems with ptr casts into ints since
you can't put an address into an int.
