As this might be of general interest. I didn't figure out an official
way to get this going either. With the the Devices->Motify/Create
Dialog of XIsso, I just couldn't enter another X-Terminal.

So I did it per hand: Add an arbitrary valid device with XIsso (say
/dev/tty00) and then edit the file /etc/auth/system/ttys. Replace
all occurences of /dev/tty00 with xterminal-hostname:0 where 
xterminal-hostname is the name of your X-Terminal.

Any other solutions anyone?

Tom

