TMW> Sorry I don't know about csh, but you don't have to have 'bash';
TMW> ksh, tcsh, and I'm sure others support it.

Tim is right. Just put this in your ~/.cshrc file:

set myhost=`expr $HOST : '\([^.]*\).*'`
alias setprompt 'set prompt="$myhost `dirs` > "'
alias cd 'chdir \!* && setprompt'
setprompt

Should work for all csh-like shells. (I'm using tcsh.)
