> peng@infinite.cs.swt.edu (Wuxu Peng) writes:
>We are in the process of buying an additional tape drive for
>our new 2100 server. We are looking at the following two tapes:
>
>    1. TZ87-TA    20GB compressed
>
>    2. TZ875-NT   100GB compressed
>
>Can any of these two fit in 3.5 storagework? The last one looks
>like for Window NT.

Check your Digital Systems and Options Catalog, December 1995 Supplement,
on page 4.55.  The TZ87-TA is a tabletop version of the TZ87 (with TK50
read compatibility).  The StorageWorks version is TZ87-VA (or TZ87N-VA
without TK50 compatibility and save a few $$$).  The TZ875-NT is a tabletop
5 cartridge stacker version of the above drive.  The TZ875-NT is not
supported under WNT (assumably because there is no software to shuffle
tapes)

We use TZ87-VA as our main backup devices on 2 of our server.  Works good
lasts a long time.



