>brian street

Well, I'm probably not helping at all, but you do need to make sure that
the dd is done on the remote system and not on your current system.  dd
writes the data differently between different OS's.  So, you should be
issuing the following command to retrieve the data:

rsh "system" (cd dir; dd if=tar.file) | tar xvf -

If this is what you are currently doing, and it is still failing, then
ignore my above gibberish and listen to someone else who has pertanant
advice!  ;)

