This may not be all that helpful, although it may point you in some 
direction.  When I installed 3.2c, I found that DEC had swapped what 
was written to stdout and stderr.  Where previously the list of files 
copied went to stdout and error/status messages to 2>, now status 
messages go to stdout and the v-list goes to 2>.  

I also found that I could no longer reliably retrieve the termination 
status in an if (...) statement in /bin/sh.  My work around was to 
check the status immediately on termination.

I know neither of these is your problem, but they may be indicators of 
a whole raft of differences in new versions of tar.

