In article <4lt1oa$294@random.tpgi.com.au>,
dhinkle <dhinkle@tpgi.com.au> wrote:
>Does anyone know how to make the c shell display the current directory
>in the prompt, and change the prompt as you change directories.
>
>Digital Unix 3.2
>
>dhinkle@tpgi.com.au
>

In ~/.cshrc;

	alias cd 'cd \!*;set prompt="! `hostname|cut -d. -f1`:$cwd:t> "

...will make the prompt show;

hostname:current-dir>

This takes effect after the first "cd" command, so you may want to put a
"cd" in ~/.login....
