> fast and complete compile. No way. Seems like lots of the header files
> in cfe are screwed up.. or the elm port is a little bogon. 

No. The elm configure script gets the sigtype wrong and sets it to int.
Edit the configuration file when configure gives you the option and
change the sigtype line to sigtype='void' and then it should compile ok.

> That leads to me this question. I'm relatively new to Digital's unix
> and was wondering when DEC ships a box, do they include a functional
> compiler, or do they give you enough to tease you (and make stuff break)
> trying to get you to buy a full package? I have a DEC 2100 2/275mhz CPU
> and v3.2 of the OS. 

DEC ship you with at least 2 C compilers. The OSF/1 C compiler and the DEC C
compiler - both of which are excellent. The DEC C compiler is run using
cc -migrate and is the same as that found on other DEC platforms eg VMS. I
think it uses the GEM technology to optimise. The other compiler is just as
good but has its own optimisation step.

Don't jump to conclusions just because you haven't thought about why something
isn't working.

