In article <4mvks8$vpv@kira.cc.uakron.edu>,
David Sumitra <david@dax.cc.uakron.edu> wrote:
>I need to migrate a huge passwd file (about 10000 uids) from Ultrix 4.3
>(UPGRADE mode) to Dunix v3.2 in ENHANCED mode. I am not able to make the
>encrypted passwords from ultrix to work on Dunix. Has anyone done this?
>I shall be much grateful for any help.

The "oldcrypt" authcap field encodes in what algorithm the current
password is encrypted. The choice currently are 0 (for "bigcrypt",
the OSF/1 "grab 8 chars at a time and use ordinary crypt while
passing on the first 2 chars on to the next round as salt" algorithm
or 1 for crypt16 (the Ultrix enhanced security algorithm). Automate
the generation of authcap files for the users (you can take the
opportunity to initialise some of the other authcap fields as well
at the same time) and set u_oldcrypt#1 and the u_pwd field to the
Ultrix password. Omitting u_newcrypt leaves it as the default of 0
and means that the next time the password is changed, the OSF/1
bigcrypt algorithm will be used instead.

--Malcolm

