>On an Alphaserver 2100,
>We would like to install a Raid Controller (KZPAA-AA) with a pair
>of disks to form a mirrored system disk.

>Question: can the console firmware boot
>Digital Unix if the system disk is connected to the raid controller??

>[we haven't ordered the controller yet.]

Dear Larry,

RAID devices are supposed to be completely transparent to the
operating system, so it's no problem to boot a RAID device. Instead of
typing eg "boot dka0" you'd say "boot dra0", which would be the first
device on the RAID controller.

We ourselves have / and /usr on RAID 0+1 ... works fine!

