In article <31883EE2.59FEC2A2@rt66.com>, Kevin Barrett <kbarrett@rt66.com> 
writes:
>Does anyone know of
>a facility provided by OSF's C compiler (or the Alpha itself) to automatically
>operate on big-endian values?  Might there be a library of good (efficient)
>conversion routines we can use?  We also have to do some conversions of
>floating-point formats (IEEE/IBM).  Any response would be appreciated...

The C compiler doesn't provide this (though Fortran does if you use
unformatted I/O.)  Endian-conversion is a rather simple task, especially
when done with shifts and masks.

There is a cvt_ftof routine (see the man page for it) that will convert
between IEEE and IBM System\360 format (among others).  IBM workstations use
big-endian IEEE.  I think that cvt_ftof may even be able to do
endian-conversions on IEEE floats.

