We have an Encore Infinity R/T model 300 system (6U VME with an Alpha
SBC and reflective memory) connected via reflective memory to several
devices, including an Encore RSX machine.  It is being used primarily
as a high-throughput interface system between the devices.  Our problem
is that the Alpha's data representation is little-endian, but all the
connected devices are big-endian.  The reflective memory system does not
do conversions or swapping, so we are stuck with having to explicitly
convert any data the Alpha has to process itself.  Does anyone know of
a facility provided by OSF's C compiler (or the Alpha itself) to automatically
operate on big-endian values?  Might there be a library of good (efficient)
conversion routines we can use?  We also have to do some conversions of
floating-point formats (IEEE/IBM).  Any response would be appreciated...
Thanks!

