There are many ways to control the size of the Networker Index.
I am sure there is a tech bulletin ( avilable via fax, http, ftp, 
or email request ).  But here are the highlights :

1) The size of the indeces are directly related to how long you keep
the file/browse stuff.  If you alter that, then on the next backup of
that system, the size of the indeces will also change.  ( There is 
a way to force that, read the manpages... )
2) You can go into the client/index and reclaim space.
3) you can delete older versions of specific indecs yourself. ( Not 
recommended, unless someone has created never cyclable data.  In
which case, you can clone it off, and recycle.... )

4) if they exceed the disk size, you can always move them to where
there is more space and soft link them back....

	Hope this helps,

	Pamela Pledger

